        explanation: 'In the discrete-action form, log-sum-exp emphasizes high-Q actions. Subtracting the mean Q of data actions makes the regularizer relatively suppress overestimated regions with little support. Continuous-action implementations require sampling and density corrections; an ordinary finite sum cannot simply be taken over an infinite action space.',
