        explanation: 'The multiplier follows gradient descent. Subtracting the negative budget-excess derivative produces the plus sign. The positive-part operator projects it back to the nonnegative range. Cost above budget raises the price; cost below budget can lower it. The estimated cost must match the policy, evaluation window, and normalization convention.',
        example: 'For λ=0.5, step size 0.1, estimated cost 0.08, and budget 0.05, the updated λ is 0.5+0.1×0.03=0.503. Replacing the plus sign with a minus would lower the price when over budget, reversing the intended feedback.',
